{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1789904703164508741,"compiled_state":{"alias":"juiced-useful-shrike","assignee":null,"attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"sshsig","author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","envelope":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.opcert.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","head_sha":"8f7417079ade1132038a6e0dd24216e8c71aa706","key_id":null,"kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 2277-7043-1f63-4f5c","material: 992666f2bae47efc","material-part: children 647ea2107ca5072f 0","material-part: description 9cee8ef8c380307e 7244","material-part: description_boxes e91772ccb5e6ce5f 0","material-part: file_impact 04e5427378e6a68d 1","material-part: ticket_id 04dde7e10861c8c6 19","model: bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 2","review-phase: planning","rebar-version: 0.13.1","regver: aa61189569d34126","verified-at-sha:e84e4c5e9439bcfd27875d152de36eb40eb4f46b","dep dbc0007425a11d6175a32a418b2d24f4923276013288fd46ef5229eea8fdbcfb .github/workflows/external-integration.yml","read-set: 1","read-path: .github/workflows/external-integration.yml","currency-basis: file_impact"],"material_fingerprint":"992666f2bae47efc","merged_log_commit":"e84e4c5e9439bcfd27875d152de36eb40eb4f46b","principal":"9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65","signature":null,"signed_at":1789904703164214944}},"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b1203a878e58a0f9c31cc1b4f358dc67458f6bc317e86c18e9803cd7c70461c7","event_uuid":"2ee4d895-4fc0-47f9-82a8-f1cfe4c8f4c4","position":{"commit_sha":"7d4c6b3b7f7d417fad9dd123acf1de2e633fefef","position":"1789904227729556796-2ee4d895-4fc0-47f9-82a8-f1cfe4c8f4c4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1db555ae17ccf167cf5a67663faf7f86161d1ab64890bb64ec027cd45d2af6a6","event_uuid":"1391700d-64a3-4093-90a3-26578a185a81","position":{"commit_sha":"275d90abd31cfd2ae42bb172caa90d3b0dfc6762","position":"1789904242956516908-1391700d-64a3-4093-90a3-26578a185a81"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"14f4038b745a28327545ecfdb80be2f62e69c2be4238ade16b850d8e5d3a8acd","event_uuid":"b1794f0d-6a09-405e-9d8b-85c7affa4b35","position":{"commit_sha":"c7936e6b0698f15964409aea4fe2b9cf12019864","position":"1789904333695059684-b1794f0d-6a09-405e-9d8b-85c7affa4b35"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2b6af766705977b52ef9d0827cdd6b5a83693bd3bc9e51754020aa07cfee9184","event_uuid":"7a66c4d5-c522-44eb-b81e-e159027e370c","position":{"commit_sha":"4d78d14cea12377843aef58e38e2064b2f75a902","position":"1789904431689372080-7a66c4d5-c522-44eb-b81e-e159027e370c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dd3aa557414db5401b49e0a45a19874b6a8969cabc81ac616167bb918135165c","event_uuid":"9c81d4e1-6671-4582-beb4-3dea4b454e1e","position":{"commit_sha":"7fde37d5afcbce3e2e32fdeb86c7dc78802d7b56","position":"1789904703164508740-9c81d4e1-6671-4582-beb4-3dea4b454e1e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1789904227729556796,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1391700d-64a3-4093-90a3-26578a185a81","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6d98-28f4-946a-4016"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nThe `jira-dc-harness` job's pytest step emits **nothing** for its entire ~2-hour\nruntime, then dumps its whole log in the final second. A run in progress is therefore\nindistinguishable from a hung one, and the workflow's own calibration comment states a\ngreen duration that measurement contradicts — so the natural reading of a healthy run is\n\"this is hung\".\n\nThat is not hypothetical. **This session cancelled a healthy run because of it**\n(run [35502010162](https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/35502010162)), destroying\n1h52m of live-Jira execution and the acceptance evidence ticket `6d98-28f4-946a-4016` was\nwaiting on.\n\n### Measured evidence\n\nThe last fully green run of this job is\n[98740362395](https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33137402410) (2026-08-28). Its\npytest step ran `03:16:01Z -> 05:00:17Z` and ended:\n\n```\n74 passed, 1 skipped, 1 xfailed, 79 warnings in 6252.74s (1:44:12)\n```\n\nEvery one of the ~1,688 log lines that step produced carries a **single** timestamp,\n`05:00:16` — the step's final second. Confirmed by counting distinct timestamps across the\nstep's line range: `1`.\n\n### The calibration comment is stale, and that is what makes it dangerous\n\n`.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` (the comment block above the run at line 624)\nstates:\n\n> The step ran 2384-2635s over 63 tests across recent green runs — a ~41s mean per test —\n> so 900s is ~22x that mean.\n\nMeasured reality, from the green run above and the two most recent completed runs:\n\n| Source | Step duration | Tests | Mean/test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Comment | 2384-2635s | 63 | ~41s |\n| Green run 98740362395 (2026-08-28) | **6252.74s** | **76** | **~82s** |\n| Run 103878992643 (2026-09-14, failure) | 7610s | — | — |\n| Run 106055322393 (2026-09-20, cancelled at) | 6748s | — | — |\n\nSo the documented range understates the real one by ~2.4x, and `900s` is **~10.9x** the\nreal mean, not ~22x. An operator comparing a live run against the documented range sees\n\"6748s vs 2635s = 2.6x over, hung\" when the run is actually at **1.08x** the last green\nrun.\n\n## Root cause\n\nEstablished by single-variable experiment, not inference.\n\n**Hypothesis 1 — Python block-buffers stdout to a pipe. REFUTED.** Running the same\n3-test, 9-second suite piped to a line-timestamper with `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1` produced\noutput identical to the default: every line stamped at the final second.\n\n```\n=== DEFAULT ===            === PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 ===\n04:35:12 ...      [100%]   04:35:27 ...      [100%]\n04:35:12 3 passed in 9.02s 04:35:27 3 passed in 9.02s\n```\n\n**Hypothesis 2 — `-q` emits progress as newline-less dots, so a line-oriented consumer\nreceives nothing until the process exits. CONFIRMED.** The same suite with `-v` instead of\n`-q` streams one line per test, at the true 3-second cadence:\n\n```\n04:35:41 ...::test_a PASSED  [ 33%]\n04:35:44 ...::test_b PASSED  [ 66%]\n04:35:47 ...::test_c PASSED  [100%]\n04:35:47 ===== 3 passed in 9.02s =====\n```\n\nGitHub Actions' log reader is line-oriented and stamps a line when it reads it. Under `-q`,\npytest writes one dot per test onto a single line and emits no newline until the run\nfinishes, so Actions has no complete line to stamp until then. The `-rA` and `--durations=25`\nalready on this step are **end-of-run** reporters and cannot fill the gap.\n\n`--timeout=900 --timeout-method=thread` is not a substitute either: it bounds a single test,\nso a 76-test run can legitimately occupy far longer than any one timeout, and nothing about\nit makes progress visible.\n\n## Scope\n\nOnly the `jira-dc-harness` lane is acutely affected, and the fix is confined to it. Measured\njob durations in run 35502010162:\n\n| Job | Duration |\n|---|---|\n| **jira DC harness smoke** | **7676s** |\n| external LLM (live anthropic) | 856s |\n| external LLM (live bedrock) | 854s |\n| Pandoc corpus replay (macos) | 266s |\n| external integration (live services) | 200s |\n| langfuse tracing round-trip | 156s |\n| jira Cloud coordinator mutation probe | 52s |\n\nEvery other lane finishes in minutes, where a silent window is not an operational hazard.\nChanging all six `-q` sites would be mechanical churn against lanes that do not exhibit the\nproblem, so the other five are deliberately left alone.\n\n## Design\n\nTwo edits, both in `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`, in the `jira-dc-harness`\nstep at line 624:\n\n1. **`-q` -> `-v`** in the pytest invocation. `-rA`, `--durations=25`, `--timeout=900`,\n   `--timeout-method=thread`, `-p no:cacheprovider` and `--basetemp` are all retained\n   unchanged. `-v` is what makes each test's completion a newline-terminated line, which is\n   the mechanism proven above.\n2. **Correct the stale calibration comment** to the measured figures (6252.74s over 76\n   tests on the green run, ~82s mean, `900s` ~= 10.9x that mean), and cite the run id the\n   numbers come from so the next re-calibration has a provenance trail rather than a bare\n   assertion.\n\nNo source code changes. No new mechanism: this adds no lock, env var, config key, feature\nflag, CI gate, autouse fixture, or test helper — it changes one existing step's verbosity\nflag and one comment.\n\n## Portability\n\nThis is a change to an existing GitHub Actions workflow's own step, not a new capability\nwith a CI-specific trigger. The underlying behaviour — `pytest -v` streams per-test lines\nwhile `pytest -q` does not — is a property of pytest, identical under any CI provider or\nnone, and is reproducible locally with the experiment recorded above. Nothing here is\ngated on GitHub Actions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python scripts/check_workflow_parity.py` equivalent coverage is provided by the repo's\n  pytest-enforced CI-workflow parity tests; `make verify` runs them.\n- `make verify` must be green, with the only failures the known macOS-arm64 pandoc set.\n- The behavioural claim is proven by the recorded local experiment, which any reviewer can\n  re-run in under a minute.\n- A post-merge dispatched run of `external-integration.yml` must show the DC harness step\n  emitting per-test lines with **more than one** distinct timestamp, against the green\n  baseline's `1`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The `jira-dc-harness` pytest step in `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` uses `-v` rather than `-q`.\n- [ ] That step still passes `-rA`, `--durations=25`, `--timeout=900`, `--timeout-method=thread`, `-p no:cacheprovider`, and `--basetemp`.\n- [ ] The step's calibration comment states the measured green duration `6252.74s` rather than the stale `2384-2635s`.\n- [ ] The step's calibration comment states the measured test count `76` rather than the stale `63`.\n- [ ] The step's calibration comment cites the run id the measurement came from.\n- [ ] No other pytest invocation in `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` changes its `-q`/`-v` flag.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` passes (exit 0) with no unadmitted new or increased entry.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports no new and no increased entries.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green apart from the known macOS-arm64 pandoc failures.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A dispatched post-merge `external-integration.yml` run shows the DC harness pytest step emitting more than one distinct log timestamp.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"Change the jira-dc-harness pytest step from -q to -v so per-test progress streams, and correct the stale calibration comment to the measured green figures."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","observability","signal-quality","external-integration"],"ticket_id":"2277-7043-1f63-4f5c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Jira DC harness emits no log output for ~2 hours, so a healthy run is indistinguishable from a hang","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2ee4d895-4fc0-47f9-82a8-f1cfe4c8f4c4","1391700d-64a3-4093-90a3-26578a185a81","b1794f0d-6a09-405e-9d8b-85c7affa4b35","7a66c4d5-c522-44eb-b81e-e159027e370c","9c81d4e1-6671-4582-beb4-3dea4b454e1e"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789904703164508741,"uuid":"3550899b-4727-4885-b9ff-7e1c0baf9555"}